  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Economic Empowerment of Youth in Two High Departure Areas (Kayes and Segou) in Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the project is to create viable livelihoods and skills for youth as an alternative to irregular migration by increasing access to employment opportunities and income generating activities in high departure areas in the regions of Kayes and Segou. In view of the precarious skills profiles as well as the disadvantaged employment context facing the youth, the two regions figure among the main zones of origin of young irregular migrants from Mali. The project aims to promote skills development and entrepreneurial activities in the two regions, this enabling social and economic empowerment of youth.</narrative>
  </description>
